---
layout: article
title: Create an automation
description: Schedule a recurring Appwrite Agent prompt with a cron schedule and optional model.
---

Create an automation when you want the Agent to run the same prompt on a schedule and leave the result in a conversation you can review.

# Create {% #create %}

1. Sign in to [Appwrite Cloud](https://cloud.appwrite.io).
2. Go to `/agent/automations` (or `/agent/automations/create`).
3. Click the create action if you are on the list view.
4. Enter a **name**.
5. Write the **prompt** the Agent should run each time.
6. Set a **schedule** with the cron editor (for example weekly on Monday).
7. Optionally set a **title prefix**, choose a **model**, and confirm a **context project** if the prompt is project-specific.
8. Leave **Enabled** on, then save.

# Review a run {% #review-a-run %}

When the schedule fires, open the automation and its linked conversations to read the Agent output, tool activity, and any inline resource cards or charts.

# Update or pause {% #update-or-pause %}

1. Open the automation from `/agent/automations/{automationId}` or the automations panel.
2. Change the prompt, schedule, model, or enabled state.
3. Save your changes.

Disable the automation to pause future runs without deleting it.

{% info title="MCP for live data" %}
Automations that inspect or change project resources need [Appwrite MCP](/docs/products/agent/mcp) connected on the account that owns the automation.
{% /info %}

See [Automations](/docs/products/agent/automations) for fields and example use cases.
